# Copy to dev.env (git-ignored). `pnpm dev` and `pnpm start` read it.
#
# The signer has no TCP listener in any configuration (ADR 0020): its API
# is on this Unix socket, which the service reaches as SIGNER_SOCKET_PATH
# too. In development the socket and the store live in apps/harpocrates/.run/,
# which is git-ignored; the shared token and the unseal key are secrets, in
# HARPOCRATES_SECRETS_DIR beside the stack's (ADR 0019):
#
#   S=/Users/ncfritz/Docker/secrets/harpocrates
#   (umask 077 && openssl rand -hex 32 > $S/harpocrates_dev_signer_token)
#   pnpm dev                                   # starts sealed: uninitialised
#
# then set it up from the console (/setup), or `pnpm signer initialise`,
# which prints the unseal key: write it to harpocrates_dev_signer_unseal_key
# there; from then on it unseals itself.
#
# (`pnpm signer <command>` runs `python -m harpocrates_signer <command>`
# with this file.)
SIGNER_SOCKET_PATH=../.run/signer.sock
SIGNER_STORE_PATH=../.run/signer.db
SIGNER_TOKEN_FILE=/Users/ncfritz/Docker/secrets/harpocrates/harpocrates_dev_signer_token
SIGNER_UNSEAL_KEY_FILE=/Users/ncfritz/Docker/secrets/harpocrates/harpocrates_dev_signer_unseal_key

# How long a ceremony may hold an offline CA's key, at most 3600.
# SIGNER_CEREMONY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600

# DEBUG also turns on Uvicorn's access log.
SIGNER_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
